== Installation ==

1. Upload the plugin files to the '/wp-content/plugins/smart-searchify' directory, or install the plugin directly through the WordPress plugins screen..
2. Activate the plugin through the 'Plugins' screen in WordPress Admin Panel.

== Frequently Asked Questions ==

= How is this different from the default search functionality? =

The default search functionality lists all content and does not provide any options to filter search results. Additionally, it cannot be used on any page of your choice. Smart Searchify offers more flexibility in this regard. It allows you to generate any number of customised search forms with different configurations. For example, you can create one search form for the default post type and another for custom post types using a shortcode. These search forms can then be rendered on any page with various filtering options based on your configuration.

= Can we use multipe forms on the same page? =
Sorry, not at the moment.

